// apply_ability_verb_chronicle_consumer — closed-loop fixture combining
// the verb-body apply_ability dispatcher (apply_ability_verb_smoke.sim's
// shape) with a chronicle consumer rule (apply_ability_chronicle_consumer.sim's
// consumer half).
//
// **Structural template for task #138.** Once this works, the actual
// duel_abilities Strike swap is a mechanical port of the same pattern:
//
//   verb-body `apply_ability` → dispatcher writes EffectDamageApplied
//   → chronicle consumer reads it → agent_hp decreases per tick
//
// The two existing apply_ability fixtures
// (apply_ability_verb_smoke.sim + apply_ability_chronicle_consumer.sim)
// each prove half the chain in isolation:
//   - verb_smoke: verb-body dispatch shape (verb expander synthesises a
//     `verb_chronicle_<Name>` physics handler, kernels emit; runtime
//     pin only validates the dispatcher kernel writes records).
//   - chronicle_consumer: PerAgent dispatcher (NOT verb) + PerEvent
//     consumer + GPU agent_hp decrement closed loop.
//
// This fixture combines them: the dispatcher half is verb-driven (`Cast`
// verb whose body is `apply_ability ... by self target self` — same as
// verb_smoke), and the consumer half is the same `on EffectDamageApplied`
// PerEvent rule as chronicle_consumer.
//
// **Closed-loop kind tag (engine-aliased; fixed 2026-05-06).** The
// dispatcher writes records with the engine's hardcoded
// `EventKindId::EffectDamageApplied = 26`. Engine event names are
// aliased to their hardcoded discriminants at resolve time — see
// `dsl_ast::engine_events::engine_event_kind_id_for_name`. The
// resolver populates `EventIR::engine_kind_id`; the lowering driver's
// `populate_event_kinds` and `resolve_event_ref` both mirror that
// assignment, so the consumer's PerEvent kernel emits
// `if (kind == 26u)` directly. No build.rs sed-rewrite needed.
//
// **P6 caveat (warning, not error).** Trips the same well_formed P6
// check that `duel_abilities.sim::ApplyDamage` and
// `apply_ability_chronicle_consumer.sim::ApplyChronicleDamage` trip:
// PerEvent rules with `agents.set_hp` are flagged because P6's strict
// reading is "events are the mutation channel, PerEvent rules should
// emit events not write fields directly". `duel_abilities` tolerates
// the diagnostic at build.rs (returns `o.program` from the
// `DriverOutcome::Err` path, kernels emit anyway). The runtime crate
// for this fixture (`apply_ability_verb_chronicle_consumer_runtime`)
// uses the same pattern, and the compile-pin in
// `crates/dsl_compiler/tests/apply_ability_smoke.rs` uses
// `compile_sim_tolerating_diagnostics`.
//
// The verb's `score 1.0` is constant — argmax over a single verb
// trivially wins, so the verb fires every tick `self.alive` is true.

event Tick { }

// Engine-side chronicle event written by the apply_ability dispatcher
// (kind=26 in cascade::handler::EventKindId). Declared here so the
// PerEvent rule below can pattern-match it.
event EffectDamageApplied { actor: AgentId, target: AgentId, amount: f32 }

entity Hero : Agent { }

scoring {
  Cast = 1.0
}

// Verb-body apply_ability dispatcher. The verb expander wraps the
// ApplyAbility into a synthesised `verb_chronicle_Cast` physics handler;
// the standard physics-lowering pipeline carries it through to the
// dispatcher kernel. Mirror of apply_ability_verb_smoke.sim's verb.
verb Cast(self) =
  action Cast
  when  self.alive
  apply_ability agents.level(self) by self target self
  score 1.0

// PerEvent: chronicle consumer. Reads EffectDamageApplied records
// the dispatcher wrote into event_ring, decrements target hp by
// the chronicle's amount field. `@phase(post)` is the spec'd
// chronicle / telemetry channel — Gap X (2026-05-04) extended the
// P6 check to recognize the annotation; the diagnostic the original
// fixture was tolerating no longer fires.
@phase(post)
physics ApplyChronicleDamage {
  on EffectDamageApplied { actor: c, target: t, amount: a } {
    agents.set_hp(t, agents.hp(t) - a);
  }
}
